#' epidemicdates: impute missing symptom onsets in line lists
#'
#' Some line lists fill a missing onset date with the report date minus a
#' delay drawn from the pooled empirical onset-to-report delays of cases with
#' both dates.
#' This is back-sampling.
#' `epidemicdates` applies back-sampling and three alternatives to a real
#' line list.
#' It is the R version of the core line-list tools in the Python package
#' `epidemic_dates` and the JavaScript module `epidemic-dates.js`.
#'
#' @section Warning:
#' This code was generated by an LLM.
#' Sam Abbott has only checked the interactive page.
#' This package and its tests have not been reviewed by a person.
#' Treat the results as exploratory.
#'
#' @section Main functions:
#' - [impute_linelist()] imputes missing onsets by back-sampling, a mean
#'   shift, EM back-projection and, given a delay, a forward draw.
#' - [delay_pmf()] gives a double interval censored daily Gamma delay pmf.
#' - [correct_truncation()] corrects daily onset counts for right
#'   truncation.
#' - [weekly()] sums daily counts to weeks.
#'
#' @section Methods:
#' Take a case with a missing onset, reported on day \eqn{t}, with onset day
#' \eqn{s} and delay \eqn{d = t - s}.
#' Let \eqn{T} be the data cut-off and \eqn{g(d)} the pooled empirical delay
#' pmf of complete cases.
#'
#' Back-sampling (`backsampling`) uses \eqn{P(s \mid t) = g(t - s)}.
#'
#' The mean shift (`mean`) uses
#' \deqn{s = t - \mathrm{round}\left(\sum_d d \, g(d)\right),}
#' with halves rounded up.
#'
#' The forward draw (`fwd`) uses \eqn{P(s \mid t) = f(t - s)} for a given
#' forward delay \eqn{f}.
#'
#' EM back-projection (`em`) uses
#' \eqn{P(s \mid t) \propto \lambda(s) f(t - s)}, with the onset curve
#' \eqn{\lambda} and a static delay \eqn{f} estimated jointly, allowing for
#' right truncation at \eqn{T}.
#'
#' All methods assume onsets are missing at random given the report day.
#'
#' @references
#' Repository: <https://github.com/seabbs/epidemic-imputation-demonstration>
#'
#' Interactive page:
#' <https://seabbs.github.io/epidemic-imputation-demonstration/>
#'
#' @keywords internal
"_PACKAGE"
